course: dictionary
lesson: 10175
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word tie can mean different things, so context tells you which meaning is right. «Roll up long sleeves and tie back long hair before cooking.» Here tie means to fasten with a knot or band, so the hair stays out of the way.
explain: Tie can also be a thing you wear. «A tie is a long narrow piece of cloth worn around the neck with a shirt.» If the sentence is about a shirt or a school uniform, tie is the cloth, not an action.
explain: Tie is also used when two sides finish with the same score. «The game ended in a tie.» Nobody won, because both sides had equal scores. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: the game ended equal, and that still makes sense.
fact: Tie can be a noun (a thing, like a school tie) or a verb (an action, like tie your laces).
fact: To tie means to join with a knot or bow, as in «tie your shoelaces».
fact: A tie is also a draw, when two sides get the same score: «the game ended in a tie».
fact: «Family ties» are close links between people.
fact: Ties can also be ropes or cords that hold things, such as «tie up the boat».
exercise: «Roll up long sleeves and tie back long hair before cooking.» What does tie back mean here? | Cut it very short | Shake loose and let it fall | *Fasten with a band or knot so it stays out of the way | Wash it in warm water
exercise: «The game ended in a tie.» What does tie mean in this sentence? | One side won by a big margin | A knot in a rope | *Both sides had the same score | A long narrow piece of cloth
exercise: «A tie is a long narrow piece of cloth worn around the neck with a shirt.» Which word is a noun in this sentence? | around | worn | *tie | shirt
test: «The Rat tied it up with his handkerchief.» What is the Rat doing to the injured shin? | Singing loudly to it | Pushing it along with a pole | *Wrapping it and fastening it with a knot | Writing a letter about it
test: Family ties means: | Ways to score the same as someone else | Ropes for tying up boats | *Close links between people | Long narrow pieces of cloth
exam: «A painter is the rope at the front of a boat used to tie it up.» What does tie mean in this sentence? | Push along with a long pole | Score the same as another boat | Wear around the neck | *Fasten with a knot
